.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_EVENT_LINK_EXTRACT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_event_link_extract
.Nd collect captured data for assertions
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft void
.Fo dtfl_event_link_extract
.Fa "dtfl_event_link *l"
.Fa "void (*each)(void *ctx, const uint64_t *time, const void *rec, size_t len)"
.Fa "void *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_event_link_extract
reads every
.Em Messages
event from
.Fa l ,
groups the records by time, sorts the records within each time by the
link's record type, and calls
.Fa each
once per
.Pq time , record
pair in time-then-record order.
Progress events are ignored.
A time whose records are all empty is dropped, matching the Rust
extractor.
.Pp
This is a test helper, run after a computation has finished, to compare
the captured output against an expected multiset.
A convenient pattern captures a replayed stream into a second link and
extracts that.
.Pp
The record pointer passed to
.Fa each
is borrowed from the link and is valid only for the duration of the
call; copy it to keep it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void each(void *ctx, const uint64_t *time, const void *rec,
    size_t len) {
	size_t *count = ctx;
	(*count)++;
}

size_t n = 0;
dtfl_event_link_extract(link, each, &n);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
This function does not return error codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_event_link_replay 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_capture 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn extract
helper of
.Pa capture/extract.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Called after the computation has finished, from the thread that holds
the link.
A link made with
.Fn dtfl_event_link_new_sync
may be extracted on a thread other than the one that captured it.
